<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine Dec unemployment rises 25.5 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Ukraine Dec unemployment rises 25.5 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Registered unemployment in Ukraine rose to 351,103 at the end of December from 308,350 at the end of November, the Statistics Ministy said on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave the following data:</p>
<p> UKRAINIAN UNEMPLOYMENT	  DEC 96     NOV 96     DEC 95</p>
<p> number of unemployed	    351,103    308,350    126,853</p>
<p> mth/mth change (percent)	+25.5	+11.1	+26.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Official Ukrainian information tends to understate unemployment levels.</p>
<p>Ukrainian Labor Minister Mykola Biloblodsky previously said that registered unemployment stood at about 0.9 percent of the work force, but also said that real unemployment stood at about 3.5 million. Ukraine's work force is estimated at 27.7 million.</p>
<p>The government has forecast registered unemployment to rise to 1.3 million by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Kiev Newsroom, +380 44 229 2264</p>
</text>
